Written by zvtt in Plan 9 from light-garden's canon-prelude.ndjson.
Each cue's identifier is its source file and line. A cue is one animation
frame, in canon order: its second is the frame, not a clock (SPEC-07 I-79); the
canon's UTC t and timestamp stay out. Over each cue's first 11 code points, ruby: in Aegean its
XOR with R0's zeroth (YHWH, YAHWEH, ADONAI, turned by PL360), joined by R0's
separator; in braille its bytes XOR the nearest of GOD IS WORD, WORD IS GOD,
GOD OF WORD, WORD OF GOD, whose IS or OF sets FLAG for the turn.
Each voice's colour is its hue on the dome; its number, and so its region,
is read from the camera (turn 0, clockwise): the hues' order seen from it, the
camera itself, OBSERVER, with no hue, last.

